1 STYLE FIGHTSTYLE FIGHTSTYLES~
Syntax: style
Syntax: style <evasive|defensive|standard|offensive|agressive>

STYLE lets you pick how you fight. Typing STYLE alone shows your current
scores in each style; typing STYLE with an option switches your active
style:

  Evasive    - trades hitroll and damroll for a much better armor class,
               favoring not getting hit at all
  Defensive  - a milder version of evasive: better armor class and a
               smaller hitroll/damroll tradeoff
  Standard   - no bonuses or penalties either way
  Offensive  - trades armor class for better hitroll and damroll
  Agressive  - a stronger version of offensive: bigger hitroll/damroll
               gain, at a steeper cost to armor class

Each style has its own skill that grows on its own the more you fight
while using it - the longer you stick with a style, the more it pays off.
Your style skills are capped by your Combat ability (Martial Artists and
Combat-class characters get a higher cap).
~

