This allows all the junkies to get there fix.
~

1 TRACTORBEAM~
Syntax: tractorbeam <ship name>

Attempts to capture a smaller ship in the same system into your ship's
hangar. Requires an installed tractor beam module, an open bay, and
enough energy on hand. You must be in the cockpit and pilot's seat, and
your ship must not be disabled, docked, or in hyperspace.
~

1 TEACH~
Syntax : teach <player> <skill>

If you have a skill at adept (100%) you may teach it to another player.
Player must be able to practice skill normally to be taught.
~

1 TARGET~
.
Syntax : Target (ship name)
 
Used in ship to ship combat to target enemy ships.
 
See also help Space Combat 1, help Weapon Syatems.
~

101 TARGETTYPES~
.
Target                Function
--------------------------------------------------------------------
ignore                Spell affect relies on the casting argument
offensive             Spell will initiate combat
defensive             Can be cast on anyone safely
self                  Spell only affects the caster
objinv                Casted onto an object in the caster's inventory
~

0 TELEPORT~
Syntax: feel <teleport>

This power takes you from your current location to a random location somewhere
in the world.
~

1 THIEF THIEVES~
~

0 THIEF THIEVES~
The thief is a dark character which makes use of many skills often deemed
improper by the rest of society.  The skills of the thief reflect his way
of life, namely sneaking in the dark, picking locks, and attacking from
behind with deadly backstabs.  Thieves have always had a bad reputation
so don't be suprised if you are always under suspicion.  Thieves start off
fairly weak, but as they gain skills such as backstab and circle they soon
become dangerous foes.  A thief is always usefull when there is a lock
that needs opening or an item that needs to be stolen.
 
~

101 THINK~
Syntax:  think <message>
 
Allows you to use the 'think' channel, which functions the same as all
other channels and can only be seen by those of high enough level.
The level for access to think can be controlled with 'cset'.
 
See CSET
~

1 THROW~
&WSyntax&w: throw <object> [direction] [target]
&w
&wThrows whatever you are holding or wielding, either at the floor, at a
target in the same room, or through an exit into an adjoining room.
Heavier objects tend to produce more damaging results.
&w
&wThe weapon you throw matters. If it matches one of the throwing
specializations (saber_throwing, dagger_throwing, axe_throwing,
spear_throwing, entangling_throw), that skill boosts your accuracy and
reduces wear on the weapon when it lands. deadeye adds a further damage
bonus on top of that, regardless of what you are throwing.
&w
&wThrown melee weapons normally land in the room. With telekinetic_throwing
you have a chance to pull the weapon straight back into your hand instead
- it will never work on grenades.
&w
&WSee Also&w: grenades, saber_throwing, dagger_throwing, axe_throwing,
spear_throwing, entangling_throw, telekinetic_throwing, deadeye
~

1 SILVERTONGUE~
Syntax: silvertongue

Silvertongue is an interesting ability unique to only the swiftest of
tongues. This skill gives the user the ability to haggle their way into
getting a better deal no matter where they go.
~

1 DIPLOMATIC_IMMUNITY "DIPLOMATIC IMMUNITY" DIPLOMATICIMMUNITY~
Syntax: diplomatic_immunity

Diplomatic Immunity is an ability reserved for the best of diplomats.
Through their status, they prove themselves above the law, and will not
receive planetary wanted flags for killing citizens. It is a passive
perk of high diplomatic standing, not a skill that can be practiced or
learned directly.
~

1 MASKAURA~
Syntax: feel 'maskaura'

Maskaura, in short, makes your auras completely invisible to detection.
Where one would normally see your auras with the detections, a masked
aura will go by completely unnoticed. On this server it also hides your
alignment reading from intelligence-gathering skills while you're dark
side aligned.
~

0 REGENERATION~
Syntax: feel 'regeneration' [target]

Regeneration speeds up your healing rate quite a bit. Anyone with
regeneration will see a LARGE gain in hp/mv regeneration. The actual
bonus is 4x as effective.
~

1 DUCK~
This skill is the equal to dodge but for smugglers, allowing you to evade
an enemy's attack by means of ducking. Use of this skill is automatic
through battles.
~

1 DEFLECT~
Deflect is a reflexive jedi skill in regards to lightsaber fighting. While
wielding a lightsaber, a jedi can reflexively bounce back a blaster bolt
with little or no problems whatsoever. This bolt does lose some energy in
the transformation and so will actually do less damage than if it were to
hit its original target. In order for a blaster bolt to be deflected, it
must first be parried. Not all blaster bolts parried will be deflected, or
at least back at the shooting party.
~

1 DEADEYE~
Syntax: reflexive

Deadeye gives you an edge when it comes to using thrown weapons. Thrown
weapons are far more likely to hit, and cause far more damage than
normal, due to the precise hand-eye coordination of the trained espionage
agent.
~

1 BATTLECRY~
Syntax: battlecry

Battlecry is an effective form of boosting morale within a group. It
affects every person within your group, and usually lasts until the
fight ends. To take advantage of battlecry you must be in the same group.
~

1 GEMCUTTING~
Syntax: gemcutting [item]
Requirements: toolkit, oven, crystal

This skill allows the engineer to try and get a perfect cut of a gemstone,
effectively doubling its worth. It is a long process, with a low chance
for success - however, as anyone can tell you, a perfectly cut gemstone
is truly a beautiful and powerful gemstone. A failure at gemcutting
results in a useless gemstone.
~

1 IMPROVED_CONCENTRATION "IMPROVED CONCENTRATION"~
Improved concentration is a passive item skill that raises your odds of
success on certain fine engineering and medical work. It currently boosts
the chances (and the skill cap) of gemcutting, and the chances of
successful medicine concentration.
~

1 "FIGHTER PILOT" FIGHTERPILOT FIGHTER_PILOT~
Fighter pilots are crazy ass pilots that completely own the
skies, they are well known for piloting their starfighters and being
victorious in all forms of space combat.

&R- &G+3 Base Damage Bonus on Laser and Ion Cannons
&R- &GMissiles fired at one class stronger than actual. For example
missiles become as strong as torpedos, torpedos become as strong as
rockets, and rockets become as strong as heavy space bombs
(Only in theory, space bombs are not attainable.)&w
&R-&G 5% bonus to Evade
~

1 ASSASSIN~
&wAn assassin, is nothing more than an experienced murderer. They often use
death attacks as their primary focus, therefore are swift and deadly. They
are also often hard to find, as they either fit in well with the people,
or know how to stick in shadows extremely well.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G Bounty hunting level 100.
&w
&GBenefits: 
&R-&G 1.5x backstab/circle damage
&R-&G Immune to research_target.
&R-&G Immune to gather_intelligence.
&R-&G Poisoned weapons do not deteriorate.
~

1 DOCTOR~
&wDoctors are extremely good at preparing medications and administering
them with ease. There is no such thing as a doctor who isn't useful, for
one thing or another. Even the best of medics, may be supplied by doctors,
because the quality of a doctor is unsurpassed.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G Medical level 100.
&w
&GBenefits:
&R-&G 50% added potency to refined medicines.
~

1 'FALSE PROPHET' FALSE_PROPHET FALSEPROPHET~
&wThe False Prophet is one that has bound themselves to the will of
the force. Or so they would claim anyway. Sometimes people will
allude to them as the Gray Jedi, others call them heretics and 
fiends. They are open to using all force powers, regardless of 
how vile they may appear on the surface. The Force is NOT inherently
evil in their minds. 
&w 
They may or may not be evil, but the branding of evil never fades
from dabbling in the dark side. Because of their unwillingness to
commit firmly to a code they have lack the zeal that empowers true
jedi and sith masters. 
&w 
&RRequirements: 
&R-&G General level 100 
&R-&G Force level 75 
&R-&G Alignment of -400 or lower 
&w  
&GBenefits:
&R-&G Ability to use all force spells. 
&R-&G Alignment cannot go higher than -400. 
&w
&RPenalties:
&G-&R Force powers are significantly weaker. 
~

1 FORCESENSITIVE FORCE_SENSITIVE "FORCE SENSITIVE"~
&wEver feel like you were unnaturally lucky? Hard training never 
seemed to do much, but a little bit of luck has seen force sensitives
through the day. At the cost of an advanced subclass, a player can opt
instead to be a force sensitive player. 
 
&RWARNING: 
&wPlayers that take this subclass are cloned immediately 
after taking it. Only take this subclass if you are serious about it.
 
&RRequirements: 
&R- &GMain class level 100.
&R-&G Force level must be no higher than 1.
 
&GBenefits:
&R- &G25-100 force levels. 
&R- &G700 force points.
&R- &G5% saving throw bonus. 
~

1 JACKOFALLTRADES JACK_OF_ALL_TRADES "JACK OF ALL TRADES"~
&wA jack of all trades, does a little bit of everything. They know a little
bit of everything, but typically are never actually skilled in any one
particular class.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&GGeneral level 100.
&w
&GBenefits: 
&R-&G +10 to all levels, except force.
~

1 JEDI~
&wSome people feel like they are jedi, whether they are or not. But it
is not unheard of for devotion to a way of life to produce results; 
after all, the force is a part of everything. Through blind devotion 
to the way of the jedi, you can force open the path to the usage of 
the force.
 
&RWARNING: 
&wPlayers that take this subclass are cloned immediately 
after taking it. Only take this subclass if you are serious about it.
 
&RRequirements: 
&R- &GMain class level 100.
&R- &GAlignment of 400 or higher.
 
&GBenefits: 
&R-&G 30-100 force levels.
&R-&G 1000 force points.
&R-&G Improved force regeneration.
&R-&G Alignment cannot fall below 400.
~

1 "SITH HUNTER" SITH_HUNTER SITHHUNTER~
&wSith Hunters have turned the hunt itself into a dark art, tracking prey
across the galaxy with a lightsaber in one hand and a blaster in the
other. Where a Jedi seeks balance, a Sith Hunter seeks the kill - and
their reflexes with a blade are honed as much for deflecting incoming
fire as for striking true.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G Bounty hunting level 100.
&R-&G Alignment of -400 or lower.
&w
&GBenefits:
&R-&G Higher deflect chance than other Force-sensitive subclasses when
wielding a lightsaber against blaster fire.
&R-&G Combat and Force levels both contribute to deflect and parry
effectiveness.
&w
&WSee also&w: deflect, parry, jedi
~

1 MARTIAL_ARTIST "MARTIAL ARTIST" MARTIALARTIST~
&wMaster of the fist, Martial Artists are powerful at fighting without a
weapon. They are capable of landing an incredible amount of blows, with
far more damage than a normal person unarmed, but they lack skill with
weapons.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G Combat level 100.
&w
&GBenefits:
&R-&GHit with fists like people hit with weapons.
&R-&GGain access to stun command.
&R-&G2 bonus attacks per round while unarmed.
&R-&GCan only wield unarmed weapons.
&R-&GDisarm Unarmed.
&R-&GExtra damage on unarmed related skills.
&R-&G250 AC bonus.
~

1 MECHANIC~
&wMechanics are the cream of the crop when it comes to maintaining crafts
of any type. Their intuition gained from working on craft has allowed them
to better pilot vehicles. To become great mechanics they have also a very
strong engineering background, which is intuitive to their nature though
not necessarily their focus.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G General level 100.
&R-&G Engineering level 25.
&w
&GBenefits:
&R-&G +25 Engineering levels.
&R-&G +25 Piloting levels.
&R-&G Improved effectiveness of ship maintenance.
~

0 MEDICAL MEDIC~
Medics, are the alchemists of the galaxy. They provide services to the
people that need such services, as they are the greatest alchemists for
potions and herbs of such a variety that most could not possibly
understand. The most experienced medical personnel can easily be the very
thing that saves your life in an instant at the moment of negative health.
They can also be your murderer, if they inject you with a vile poison. The
level bonuses for being a medic are as follows: 
&R-&G+100 Medical Levels
&R-&G+50  Combat Levels
~

1 PARAMEDIC~
&wParamedics are the insane, of the insane. They are trained to enter
combat like situations, especially anything that spills out on the
streets. They are very dedicated to their work, and can heal anyone in
even the most dire of circumstances. They were trained for one thing, and
one thing alone,  saving lives quickly and efficiently.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G Medical level 100.
&w
&GBenefits:
&R-&G Medical applications work during battle.
~

1 PRODIGY~
&wThe ways of the force are numerous, and it is quite easy to become
engulfed within them. The true tricks of the force require bending them
to your will, without excessive amounts of coercion. A natural force 
user can become far more powerful than even a grandmaster with simple 
coercion, rather than a master's discipline. Prodigy's are capable 
of doing such a thing. Their powers are stronger and maybe even 
impossible to resist.  
 
&RRequirements: 
&R- &GGeneral level 100 
&R- &GForce level 75 
 
&GBenefits: 
&R- &GExtremely powerful spells.
&R- &GMassive force regeneration.
~

1 SENATOR~
&wSenators, once a time honored tradition are making their way back into
the global economy. These typically elected officials got their positions
by knowing how to manipulate the public at advanced rates. Whether it be
simple pandering to bribery, or perhaps even simple charisma no one can
deny their diplomatic prowess.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G Diplomacy level 100.
&w
&GBenefits:
&R-&GPlanetary diplomatic skills are twice as effective.
&R-&G Diplomatic immunity (see help diplomatic_immunity).
~

1 SNIPER~
&wSnipers are the masters of long range combat. They know how to sit back
from the battlefield and late fate take its course. When the chance for
the perfect shot comes, their aim strikes true. All thats left after that
is a corpse. 
&w 
&RRequirements:
&R-&GCombat level 100
&w
&GBenefits:
&R->en room range for sniping and scanning.
&R->ripple snipe.
&R-&GChance for a one hit kill with a sniper rifle.
~

1 SOLDIER~
&wA soldier is the very definition of a fighter. Everything they do is
compounded by combat. No matter what profession they choose, they focus on
combat heavily. Anyone can be a soldier, but not everyone is a good
soldier.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G General level 100.
&R-&G Combat level 25.
&w
&GBenefits:
&R-&G +25 Combat levels.
&R-&G +25 Bounty Hunter levels.
~

1 SWORDSMAN~
&wThe swordsman is a master of swordplay. They have mastered the
sword down to the most basic fundamentals. Their sheer speed is
unsurpassed by the unwashed masses, and their superior reflexes
allow them to parry attacks with ease.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&GCombat level 100
&w 
&GBenefits:
&R-&G 50% bonus max skill lightsabers and swords
&R-&G 25% bonus to parry regardless of skill.
&R-&G 3x critical hit with sword/saber.
&R-&G Gain access to slice command.
~

1 TAILOR~
&wTailors are engineers, dedicated to crafting sturdy clothing throughout
the galaxy.  Their clothing is much sturdier than most, and none can deny
that their work is simply sublime.  From the shortest shorts, to the best
gemcut diamonds. None can do it better than a tailor. &w
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G Engineering level 100.
&w
&GBenefits:
&R-&G 10% bonus to all armor crafting skills.
&R-&G 10% bonus to succeed on gemcutting.
~

0 TANK~
&wTanks are the 'tough guys' of the galaxy.  Strong and able to soak
incredible amounts of punishment, tanks are capable in any sort of ground
combat situation.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&GCombat level 100.
&w
&GBenefits: 
&R-&G +250 HPS
&R-&G 250 point bonus to AC
&R-&G 25 points of Damage Reduction
~

1 THIEF~
&wThieves know how to move in the shadows, and have gained extreme skills
at cutting purses from their experiences. Even the most unskilled thief is
a danger to the nearest wallet.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G Smuggling level 100.
&w
&GBenefits:
&R-&G Steal has a 50% bonus to evading getting caught.
&R-&G Steal effectiveness cap is raised 20%.
&R-&G Immune to research_target.
&R-&G Immune to gather_intelligence.
~

1 QUICKWORKER "QUICK WORKER" QUICK_WORKER~
&wQuick Workers have spent time and effort finding little shortcuts to
enable them to complete full quality work in less time. You won't find a
faster custom job anywhere. 
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&GEngineering level 100.
&w
&GBenefits: 
&R-&G Engineering crafting skills require 1/4 the time.
~

1 WEAPONSMITH~
Weaponsmiths, are engineers that are devoted to finding more inventive ways
to craft weapons. They just love making weapons, and it gives them an
extra proficiency that just isn't seen much anymore. They are dedicated
solely to crafting the best weapons in the galaxy.
&w
&RRequirements:
&R-&G Engineering level 100.
&w
&GBenefits: 
&R-&G 10% bonus to all weapons crafting.
~

1 SABER_THROWING "SABER THROWING" DAGGER_THROWING "DAGGER THROWING" AXE_THROWING "AXE THROWING" SPEAR_THROWING "SPEAR THROWING"~
&wThese skills all act as modifiers of the throw skill. Throwing with these
skills becomes far more effective than if you did not have them. They are
similar to weapon skills. They also stack with deadeye.
&w
&WSee Also&w: throw
~

1 ENTANGLING_THROW "ENTANGLING THROW"~
&wAn entangling throw is a throw that aims to immobilize a target. It is
only possible with whip and chain style weapons, as they literally wrap
around their targets. Note that this is not a form of binding, as the
weapon used can simply be removed. However, because of its nature for
entangling, it also heavily encumbers the target. This means that it
damages the movement of your target directly.
&w
&YSyntax&w: You must be wielding a whip-type weapon to throw with this
effect.
&w
&wIt also shares traits similar to the other weapon throwing skills, in
that it raises the effectiveness of throwing whip or chain style weapons.
&w
&WSee also&w: throw
~

1 TELEKINETIC_THROWING "TELEKINETIC THROWING"~
&WSyntax&w: reflexive
&w
&wTelekinetic throwing is a special force power that modifies the throwing
skill. Instead of simply losing your weapon, with telekinetic throwing you
have the opportunity to retrieve your thrown object, instead of leaving it
in the dirt.
&w
It will not return grenades to you, but will return anything else.
&w
&WSee Also&w: throw
~

1 VIBRO-AXES "VIBRO AXES" VIBRO_AXES~
&wVibro-axes are the weapon proficiency skill for wielding vibro-axes in
combat. Like the other weapon proficiency skills (vibro-blades,
vibro-swords, bludgeons, bowcasters, etc.), the better trained you are,
the more accurate and effective your attacks with a vibro-axe become.
&w
&WSee also&w: vibro-blades, vibro-swords, bludgeons
~

0 TICK~
Many of the actions in the game are based upon interval timers, including
combat, most autonomous monster actions, hp/force/move regeneration, power
duration, weather, and area resetting.
 
Of these timers, the hp/force/move regeneration timer is popularly called the
'tick'.  Ticks in the game average 30 seconds of real time, but the actual
amount varies randomly from 15 seconds to 45 seconds.
 
Area resetting happens roughly every 3 minutes if there are no characters in
in the area; less often (15 minutes) if any characters are present.  Also
note that objects lying on the ground will not be regenerated if anyone
is in the area when it resets.
 
Area resets are indicated by 'squeaking noises' just prior to the reset.
~

101 TIMECMD~
Syntax:  timecmd <command>
Example: timecmd mpstat <mob>
 
Returns the time required to execute the specified command for that
instance of its execution.
~

0 TITLE~
Syntax: title <string>

Sets your title to a given string.

The game supplies a title when your character is created and when you
advance a level.  You can use TITLE to set your title to something else.
~

101 TONGUE TONGUES~
The different languages include common, wookiee, twilek, rodian, hutt, 
mon calamari, noghri, ewok, gamorrean, jawa, adarian, verpine, defel,
trandoshan, chadra-fan, quarren and duinuogwuin.
~

1 TOPICS~
Additional topics you may want to look over:
*TICK
*WIZLIST
*EXPERIENCE
*EQDAMAGE
*CLANS
*CHANGES
*DAMAGE
*NEWS
*STORY
 
To view a topic type: HELP <topic>
~

1 TORTURE~
Syntax : Torture (mob/player)

This handy skill allows you to permenatly remove hit points from
a mob or player. 
~

0 TRACK~
Syntax: track <mob>

Track will assist you in tracking down a mob that is within the area, 
giving you its general direction. This can also be used to track 
other players.
~

1 TRAIN~
Syntax :  Train (stat)
 
Training is the only way to perminatly improve a characters
starting stats. Train can only be done with a few mobs
around the mud and is only about 20% effective.
There is no cost for training, just the long time it takes.
If you input ANY commands during training the training will
be aborted.
~

1 TRANCE~
Syntax:  trance
 
A character in possession of this skill may use it to briefly focus its
energies toward restoring a small burst of force.
~

1 TRANDOSHAN TRANDOSHA DOSHA~
These humanoid reptiles are native to the planet Trandosha. They have long 
arms, which end in wide, splayed fingers. Their heads are blunt, with beady red 
eyes and a mouth full of sharp teeth. Their scales range in color from orange 
to ochre to brown. Much of their body can be regenerated if lost, so a 
Trandoshan can fight much harder without risk of permanent injury. Being a 
vicious, warlike race, the Trandoshans evolved into hunters, and were 
especially proficient at hunting Wookiees, which inhabited the nearby planet of 
Kashyyyk. It was a Trandoshan official who sold the idea of enslaving Wookiees 
rather than simply leveling Kashyyyk to the Empire.
~

101 TRANSFER~
Syntax: transfer <character>
Syntax: transfer all
Syntax: transfer <character> <location>
Syntax: transfer all         <location>

TRANSFER transfers the target character, or ALL player characters,
to your current location (default) or to a specified location.
~

101 TRAPFLAGS~
Flags to describe a trap and what triggers it:

ROOM    - Trap is in a room
OBJ     - Trap is on an object
ENTER   - Trap is triggered by entering the room
LEAVE   - Trap is triggered by leaving the room
OPEN    - Trap is triggered by opening
CLOSE   - Trap is triggered by closing
GET     - Trap is triggered by getting the object
PUT     - Trap is triggered by putting the object
EXAMINE - Trap is triggered by examining the object
PICK    - Trap is triggered by picking the object
UNLOCK  - Trap is triggered by unlocking the object
NORTH   - Trap is triggered by moving north
SOUTH   - Trap is triggered by moving south
EAST    - Trap is triggered by moving east
WEST    - Trap is triggered by moving west
UP      - Trap is triggered by moving up
DOWN    - Trap is triggered by moving down

See RESET, TRAPSETTING and TRAPTYPES.
~

101 TRAPSETTING~
Setting a trap is a little tricky.

Parameters: <vnum> <type> <charges> <flags>
VNUM    - The vnum of either the room or object to be trapped.
TYPE    - The type of trap.  (See TRAPTYPES)
CHARGES - The number of charges this trap should contain.
FLAGS   - Flags specifying the characteristics of the trap.
          (ie: room trap or object trap, what triggers the trap, etc.)

See RESETS, TRAPTYPES and TRAPFLAGS.
~

101 TRAPTYPES~
Types of traps:

 --------------------------------------------------------------------
 | Number | Description             | Number | Description          |
 --------------------------------------------------------------------
 |    1   | Poison gas              |    8   | Flame                |
 |    2   | Poison dart             |    9   | Explosion            |
 |    3   | Poison needle           |   10   | Acid Spray           |
 |    4   | Poison dagger           |   11   | Electric Shock       |
 |    5   | Poison arrow            |   12   | Blade                |
 |    6   | Blindness gas           |   13   | Sex change power     |
 |    7   | Sleeping gas            |        |                      |
 --------------------------------------------------------------------

See RESET, TRAPSETTING and TRAPFLAGS.
~

101 TRIGGER~
A trigger is an action, phrase, or game event that causes a program
held within a room, mob or object, to begin playing out its commands.
 
Triggers can be anything from a player or mob entering a room, to a
player stating a particular phrase within a room, or to a mob or an
object.
 
For detailed information on triggers, see:
 
RPTRIGGERS, MPTRIGGERS, OPTRIGGERS
~

101 'TRUE SIGHT'~
Syntax:  feel 'true sight'
 
This power can only be cast upon yourself.  It is a combination of
infravision (enabling you to see in the dark), detect invisible,
and detect hidden.  This power also allows you to see through
blinding attacks.
~

101 TRUST~
Syntax: trust <character> <level>

TRUST sets a character's trust to the specified level.  This is similar to
advancing the character for accessing immortal commands, but has no effect
on combat strength, et cetera.  You can give more trust to mortal (or
immortal) characters to give them access to more power without messing up
the character.  You can also restrict a player's trust to less than their
natural level.

A trust of 0 means to use the character's natural level again.
~

