101 SETFORCEROLL~
Syntax: setforceroll [percent]

Setforceroll controls the flat percent chance, applied on every ability
level-up a player earns, for the Force Awakening system to trigger and
grant (or increase) that character's Force sensitivity.

Typed with no argument, it reports the current chance. Typed with a
number, it sets the chance to that value immediately and saves the
change to disk right away. There is no bounds checking - be careful,
values outside a sane 0-100 range will still be accepted and applied
literally.

This does not affect the character-creation Force roll, and does not
affect Hunters' exclusion from that creation roll - it only governs
the ongoing, per-level-up chance available to every class, Hunters
included.
~

1 "RESEARCH TARGET" RESEARCH_TARGET RESEARCHTARGET~
Syntax: research_target [player]

  Researching a player gives some insight into them. For example, if I were
to research a bounty hunter I'd find out he was a bounty hunter, and a
small list of his statistics might be. This gives me some insight into
whether I'd like to fight them, or I would not like to fight them, etc.
This does not give a full statsheet, just a small list for some small
forms of insight. It doesn't even reveal if the player is disguised or
not. 
~

1 "TRACE COMLINK" TRACECOMLINK TRACE_COMLINK~
Syntax: trace_comlink

This skill lets you trace the location of anyone talking over the "chat"
channel while it is active. On success, it reveals the planet the speaker
is currently on. Activating trace_comlink does not affect any other
channel.
~

1 ABDICATE~
Syntax: Abdicate 
 
Abdicate is a command for leaders of a clan to step down from the 
leadership position. The command completly kicks the leader from 
the clan, to re-join he/she/it must enlist or re-inducted. 
 
See Also: Appoint, Induct, Outcast, Resign, Overthrow, Abdicate. 
~

1 "ADD PATROL" "ELITE PATROL" ADDPATROL ADD_PATROL ELITEPATROL ELITE_PATROL~
&WSyntax&w: add_patrol 
&WSyntax&w: elite_patrol
&w 
&wPatrols serve the purpose of essentially being a wandering guard. To
set a patrol requires you to be part of a clan with the officer tag. 
Patrols can be dismissed. Patrols will also attack any enemies of your
clan. 
&w
&wElite_patrol is the upgraded version of add_patrol, and will provide
greater protection. There is no limit to the number of patrols you can
post, but be warned, they do get extremely spammy. 
&w
&WSee also&w: dismiss
~

1 BEEP REBEEP~
Syntax: beep <player>

Sends a short signal to another player anywhere in the world, letting
them know you'd like their attention - typically before sending a tell.
Both you and the target need a comlink carried or worn for this to work,
unless either of you is an immortal.
~

1 BESIEGE~
Syntax: besiege

Besiege is a skill used by smugglers to disable the ships autopilot, so
that they can gain access to the controls. It typically could require some
major amounts of force, and can be a trying process.
~

1 BIND~
&WSyntax&w: bind [player]
&w
&wBind is a skill that allows a player to place another player within
binding constraints. It does not inhibit movement, but it severely 
inhibits everything else. When a player is bound, they are not allowed
to resist many things, they would otherwise be able to, such as jail,
and torture.
&w
&WSee also&w: unbind, jail
~

1 BLACKJACK~
&CBlackjack&c : &GLevel 95 Smuggling Skill 
 
&CDESCRIOTION&G:&Y Blackjack is used to sneak up behind an opponent and
give him a well timed thump to the back of the head.  A successfull
blackjack will do some damage, and stun the victim.  A partially
succesfull blackjack will do some damage to the victim.  A failed blackjack
will just start a fight with a miss.
 
In order to use blackjack your MAIN weapon (not dual-wielded) must be a
bludgeon.
 
Blackjack is an agressive skill and WILL start fights.
 
&PSEE ALSO: &wSITUATIONAL_AWARENESS&P.
 
&B-=&Y Last Updated Feb 25, 2003 by Raijen &B=-&w 
~

1 BREW~
&WSyntax&w: craft_item [id] [name]  
&w
Brew is one of the various design skills associated with the 
medical class. Brews tend to be weaker than shots. The following 
item types can be crafted using brew: 
&W-&welixir     
&w 
&WRequirements vary by item, check the schematic first. 
&WSee Also&w: craft_item craft_menu schematic_info 
